## Merge Blockers

1. **Auth bypass (fail-open) on malformed or blank `expiresAt`** — [src/auth_client.ts:22-26](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts#L22-L26) ([pr_diff.patch:17-24](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L17-L24))
   - The PR removes `Number.isNaN(expiryMs)` from the expiration check. For any unparseable or whitespace-only `expiresAt`, `Date.parse(normalizedExpiry)` returns `NaN`; `nowMs >= NaN` evaluates to `false`, so `isSessionValid` returns `true` and `buildAuthContext` ([src/auth_client.ts:29-40](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts#L29-L40)) accepts the session.

2. **Runtime `TypeError` on `expiresAt: null` masked by type-check suppression** — [src/auth_client.ts:4](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts#L4), [src/auth_client.ts:20-21](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/auth_client.ts#L20-L21) ([pr_diff.patch:9](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L9), [pr_diff.patch:19-20](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L19-L20))
   - `SessionToken.expiresAt` is widened to `string | null`, but `isSessionValid` never guards against `null`. Instead, `// @ts-ignore` and `(token.expiresAt as any).trim()` silence TypeScript and throw `TypeError` at runtime when `expiresAt` is `null`.

3. **Leftover `breakpoint()` in production retry loop** — [src/retry_worker.py:41-43](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L41-L43) ([pr_diff.patch:75-77](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L75-L77))
   - Any job reaching `attempts >= MAX_ATTEMPTS` (`5`) drops the worker into an interactive debugger (`pdb`), hanging or crashing the background process.

4. **Hardcoded local developer path for signing key** — [src/retry_worker.py:10](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L10), [src/retry_worker.py:14-16](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L14-L16), [src/retry_worker.py:37](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L37) ([pr_diff.patch:38](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L38), [pr_diff.patch:42-44](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L42-L44), [pr_diff.patch:71](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L71))
   - `SIGNING_KEY_PATH = Path("/Users/dev/keys/staging.pem")` hardcodes a workstation-specific staging path, and `process_retry_batch` calls `load_signing_key()` with no override or env-var configuration, failing with `FileNotFoundError` in any other environment.

5. **Blanket `except Exception:` silently swallows all DB/query errors** — [src/retry_worker.py:21-28](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L21-L28) ([pr_diff.patch:54-61](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L54-L61))
   - `fetch_pending_jobs` catches every `Exception` and returns `[]` with no logging, metrics, timeout discrimination, or backoff—silently hiding auth failures, SQL/schema bugs, and database outages as an empty queue.

6. **Unclaimed `SELECT` allows concurrent double delivery (pre-existing, exacerbated by skipped test)** — [src/retry_worker.py:22-25](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L22-L25), [src/retry_worker.py:36-46](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L36-L46)
   - Despite the docstring ("Claim and dispatch due retry jobs"), `fetch_pending_jobs` executes a plain `SELECT` with no row lock (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`) or atomic lease/claim update; concurrent workers will fetch and dispatch the same jobs twice.

7. **Tautological mock-only test (`test_dispatch_retry_calls_handler`)** — [tests/test_worker.py:20-24](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/tests/test_worker.py#L20-L24) ([pr_diff.patch:99-103](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L99-L103))
   - Calls `mock_dispatch(...)` directly and asserts on the mock itself without ever importing or invoking `process_retry_batch` ([tests/test_worker.py:9](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/tests/test_worker.py#L9)). Provides zero coverage of dispatch, signing-key loading, `MAX_ATTEMPTS`, or `mark_delivered`.

8. **Concurrency test disabled with `@pytest.mark.skip` (and does not test concurrency)** — [tests/test_worker.py:27-37](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/tests/test_worker.py#L27-L37) ([pr_diff.patch:106-109](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L106-L109))
   - `@pytest.mark.skip(reason="flaky in CI")` suppresses the test instead of addressing the defect. Even when enabled, it only returns canned `side_effect` values sequentially on a `MagicMock` without exercising concurrent execution or claiming logic.

9. **Breaking signature change to `process_retry_batch` with zero test coverage** — [src/retry_worker.py:31-35](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L31-L35), [src/retry_worker.py:44](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/src/retry_worker.py#L44) ([pr_diff.patch:66-67](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L66-L67), [pr_diff.patch:78-79](file://<TMP_WORKSPACE>/benchmarks/sources/se2_pr_audit/pr_diff.patch#L78-L79))
   - `dispatcher` changed from `(job) -> bool` to `(job, signing_key) -> bool`, with no caller updates and no tests covering `process_retry_batch`, `load_signing_key`, `fetch_pending_jobs` error handling, or `src/auth_client.ts`.

